      "description": "Watch Velez Sarsfield vs Instituto Cordoba highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 25, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina clash between Velez Sarsfield and Instituto Cordoba promised to be a tactical battle of wills. On July 25, 2026 , both sides took to the pitch with the aim of securing crucial points, creating an atmosphere of anticipation and grit from the opening whistle. A Tight Opening and the Breakthrough The match began with notable physical intensity as both teams fought for control of the midfield. the first major talking point came in the 18th minute when Matias Gallardo was shown a yellow card following a mistimed challenge, signaling that neither side was willing to give an inch. Instituto worked hard to maintain their defensive shape, but Velez Sarsfield began to find pockets of space as the interval approached. Just as it looked like the teams would head into the break level, a moment of inspiration arrived. In the 45+1 minute, Tobias Andrada delivered a sharp pass to find Manuel Lanzini , who finished clinically to break the deadlock. The goal sparked an immediate reaction of frustration from the visitors, resulting in a yellow card for Fernando Alarcon only a minute later, ending an electric first half. Tactical Shifts and Late Tension Returning for the second half, the Instituto coaching staff looked to refresh the side with several changes, including the introduction of Ignacio Mendez and Alex Veron . The game remained highly competitive, with the referee forced to intervene regularly. Claudio Baeza and Thiago Silvero were both cautioned with yellow cards in the 75th and 79th minutes respectively, reflecting the rising tension on the pitch. Velez Sarsfield managed their lead intelligently, making strategic substitutions of their own, such as bringing on Diego Valdes and Lucas Robertone . Despite late pressure from Instituto , who threw Facundo Suarez and Nicolas Guerra into the attack, the home defense stood firm. The final whistle at 90+5 minutes confirmed the victory for Velez , in a match where Lanzini’s efficiency proved to be the decisive factor."
